        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## FLUX.1 Fill [dev]: inpainting\n\nRepaints the masked area of an image with [FLUX.1 Fill [dev]](https://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/FLUX.1-Fill-dev),\nthe inpainting model of FLUX.1 [dev] (base dev leaves visible seams), the way Forge's \"Inpaint upload\" does.\n**Inpaint Crop** cuts the masked area with some context out of the image and scales it to the generation size, so that\neven a small area is sampled at full resolution; **Inpaint Model Conditioning** gives Fill the crop and its mask;\n**Inpaint Stitch** scales the result back and blends it into the original through the blurred mask. **Differential\nDiffusion** makes the soft mask edge blend gradually.\n\nRequires [ComfyUI-Inpaint-CropAndStitch](https://github.com/lquesada/ComfyUI-Inpaint-CropAndStitch) (install it with\nthe ComfyUI Manager).\n\n**Settings**: 20 steps (28 for finals), guidance **30** (Fill's own value, Distilled CFG in the Generate tab; dev's 3.5\ngives washed-out fills), euler, simple, denoising 1.0.\n\n## Image Bench\n\nThe Generate tab is in **Inpaint** mode while this workflow is loaded.\n\n| Marker / node | Generate tab |\n|---------------|--------------|\n| `ib:img` Load Image | Input cell; \"Send image\" from Photoshop |\n| `ib:mask` Load Image Mask | Mask cell; the Photoshop selection |\n| `ib:cp`, `ib:pp`, `ib:lora` | model, prompt, LoRAs (as in the other workflows) |\n| `ib:smp` SamplerCustomAdvanced | seed, steps, scheduler and denoising (BasicScheduler), sampling method, Distilled CFG |\n| Inpaint Crop | Resize to (`output_target_width/height`), Mask blur (`mask_blend_pixels`), Mask mode (`mask_invert`) |\n| Only masked padding (Grow Mask) | Only masked padding, pixels |\n| Whole picture (Solid Mask) | Inpaint area: value 0 = Only masked, 1 = Whole picture |\n\nThe loaders refer to the files the Photoshop plugin writes (`image_bench_photoshop_*.png`); send an image and a\nmask, or set them in the Input / Mask cells of the Generate tab, before the first queue.\n\n- **Only masked**: the model sees only the crop (the mask's bounding box plus the padding, widened to the aspect\n  ratio of the size). Describe what the crop shows, the new content of the masked area and its surroundings.\n- **Whole picture**: the whole image is scaled to the size and sampled; describe the whole image.\n- Fill replaces the masked content at denoising 1.0; lower values keep more of its colors and shapes.\n- Mask blur widens the mask by that many pixels and blurs it; the pixels outside the mask within that distance are\n  blended too. Keep the size near 1 MP with sides multiples of 16 (**ModelSamplingFlux** reads the crop size).\n- Outpainting: extend the canvas in the editor, mask the new area and use Whole picture or a large padding.\n- Most FLUX.1 [dev] LoRAs work on Fill too, somewhat weaker. Model exploration should list only Fill models: base\n  dev checkpoints do not take the inpaint conditioning.\n\n## Model Links\n\n**diffusion_models**: [flux1-fill-dev.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/FLUX.1-Fill-dev/resolve/main/flux1-fill-dev.safetensors)\n(gated: accept the license on the model page and download it logged in; 24 GB, choose *fp8_e4m3fn* as weight_dtype\nof the loader with less than 24 GB of VRAM)\n**text_encoders**: [clip_l.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/comfyanonymous/flux_text_encoders/resolve/main/clip_l.safetensors),\n[t5xxl_fp16.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/comfyanonymous/flux_text_encoders/resolve/main/t5xxl_fp16.safetensors)\n**vae**: [ae.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Lumina_Image_2.0_Repackaged/resolve/main/split_files/vae/ae.safetensors)\n\nFLUX.1 Fill [dev] is under the FLUX.1 [dev] non-commercial license.\n"
      ],
      "title": "Note: FLUX.1 Fill [dev] inpainting (Image Bench)",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
